    {
      "id": "kinetempo-upper-trap-stretch",
      "name": "Upper trapezius and levator stretch",
      "description": "Sit on your hand to anchor the shoulder down. For the trapezius, tip the ear toward the opposite shoulder; for the levator, turn the nose toward the armpit first and then look down. Use the free hand only as light weight on the head — no pulling. Thirty seconds a side, twice, breathing out into the stretch. It should feel like a broad pull along the side or back of the neck, never sharp, and never with pins and needles into the arm.",
      "videoUrl": null,
      "steps": [
